==Enemy==
Ragin' Gory is comparable to a buffed [[Gory Dark]], with whom he shares about all features. The core difference is that Ragin' Gory has [[Immune to Freeze|immunity to freeze]], which makes the likes of [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]], [[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Oda Nobunaga]] and the [[Ototo Corps|Thunderbolt Cannon]] useless against him. He also has slightly higher range, much higher health and 2 less knockbacks.

Ragin' Gory is far more resilient than Gory Dark, but his attack power isn't much higher by comparison. A 100% Ragin' Gory has just 34 less health as an 803% Gory Dark and 8 less damage than a 360% Gory Dark.

==Strategy==
Ragin' Gory isn't much different from the original. Although freeze cannot be used against him, other status effects and direct damage still work. One can use a stack of mid-ranged attackers such as [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] to cripple him, or any [[:Category:Behemoth Slayer Cats|Behemoth Slayers]] that can safely attack him. [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]] can work as a [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controller]] if they don't appear in large numbers. [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|Anti-Dark]] meatshields like [[Nono (Rare Cat)|Nono]], [[Ancient Egg: N103 (Rare Cat)|Gas Mask Cat]], [[Li'l Gau (Rare Cat)|Crystal Li'l Gau Gau]] and [[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Kinjirou Cat]] can be spammed to tank him for a considerably longer time than anything else, which can be enough for your attackers to catch up.

