==Trivia==
*The term "[[wikipedia:Black company (Japan)|black company]]" (ブラック企業 ''burakku kigyō'') in Ragin' Gory's Japanese description refers to an exploitative company that is harmful to its employees' welfare, with common traits being large amounts of overtime with little or no pay, few or no days off, poor working conditions, and abuse such as power harassment, sexual harassment or maternity harassment. To get away with these violations of Japanese labor rights, black companies often hire a large number of naïve young employees, threatening them with disrepute if they choose to quit.
*Along with [[Ultima Beast Naala]] and [[Wild Doge]], Ragin' Gory was one of the three enemies that were updated to have the [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] type in [[Version 11.5 Update|Version 11.5]].
**This makes Ragin' Gory technically the first Behemoth enemy introduced, as he was the first of these three enemies to be added.
**Version 11.5 was released on April 19th, 2022, meaning Ragin' Gory was updated exactly 1 year and 1 day after his release ([[Version 10.5 Update|Version 10.5]] on April 18th, 2021).
*Since he's a Behemoth, Ragin' Gory might represent ''Monster Hunter''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s [[wikia:monsterhunter:Blango|Blango]], a highly aggressive, simian [[wikia:monsterhunter:Fanged Beast|Fanged Beast]] with the opposite fur color to Ragin' Gory (white instead of black). Unlike most other Behemoths, Ragin' Gory is a peon that often spawns in groups, similar to how Blango is a [[wikia:monsterhunter:Category:Small Monsters|Small Monster]] that hunts in packs. His Japanese name (怒りのブラッゴリ ''Ikari no Buraggori'') shares ブラ ''Bura'' (Bla) and ゴ ''go'' with Blango (ブランゴ ''Burango''), though ブラッゴリ ''Buraggori'' is just [[Gory Dark]]'s Japanese name.
**Ragin' Gory could also simply be the only Behemoth that doesn't reference ''Monster Hunter'' in any way, as he was added over a year before the Behemoth type.
*Ragin' Gory and Wild Doge are the only Behemoths whose Japanese names do not include a title with the format "Super X Beast" (超X獣 ''Chō Xjū''), where X is a prefix related to the enemy in question.
**They are also the only Behemoths to have any hiragana in their Japanese names.
*He is the only Behemoth to appear in [[The Aku Realms]] and [[Underground Labyrinth]].
*He and Gory Dark are the only variants of [[Gory]] whose descriptions don't mention their scary faces.

